-- title:
--   Sums over descendants as interval sums
-- statement:
--   Let an ordered tree have levels $\{0,\dots,s_k-1\}$ with monotone surjective parent maps, and for levels $i\le j$ let $\mathrm{anc}:\text{level }j\to\text{level }i$ be the ancestor map. For a node $v$ at level $i$, $\mathrm{lo}(v)$ is the index of its first descendant at level $j$ and $\mathrm{hi}(v)$ is one more than the index of its last. For every function $f$ on indices with values in an additive monoid,
--   $$
--   \sum_{s\text{ desc. of }v}f(s)=\sum_{i=\mathrm{lo}(v)}^{\mathrm{hi}(v)-1}f(i) .
--   $$
--
--   Descendant sums are sums over a contiguous range.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Nonexpansive/SwitchingBlocks.lean#L21-L42

